-- Scene 6: what is REFUSED, and why --
  [ok]   a file that is not MIDI: refused -- MIDI: not a Standard MIDI File -- it does not begin with MThd
  [ok]   format 2 (independent sequences, not one piece): refused -- MIDI: format 2 holds independent sequences, not one piece; formats 0 and 1 are read
  [ok]   SMPTE time, not beats: refused -- MIDI: the file counts SMPTE frames, not beats; only beat-timed files are read
  [ok]   a track cut inside a message: refused -- MIDI: track 1 ends inside a message
  [ok]   an ABC tune with no K: line: refused -- ABC: music before the K: line -- a tune's header ends with K:, and this one has none
  [ok]   an empty text: refused -- ABC: the text is empty

-- What the readers do NOT do --
   MusicXML is not read (it was not asked for). MIDI: one tempo per score, no pedal, no
   controllers beyond the bend's range; a moving bend is a glide, so vibrato is flattened.
   ABC: no ornaments, dynamics, lyrics, grace notes or chord symbols (each COUNTED when
   met); no nested repeats and no P: parts order; one tune per text.

